<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!DOCTYPE task PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA Task//EN" "task.dtd">
<task id="adjusting-image-repository-visibility-the-api">
  <title>Adjusting repository visibility by using the API</title>
  <shortdesc>To control who can pull or interact with a repository, you can set its visibility to public or private by using the Red Hat Quay API.</shortdesc>
  <taskbody>
    <prereq>
      <ul>
        <li>You have <xref href="https://docs.redhat.com/en/documentation/red_hat_quay/3.18/html-single/red_hat_quay_api_guide/index#creating-oauth-access-token" format="html" scope="external">Created an OAuth access token</xref>.</li>
        <li>You have created a repository.</li>
      </ul>
    </prereq>
    <context>
      <p>The visibility of your repository can be set to <codeph>private</codeph> or <codeph>public</codeph> by using the <xref href="https://docs.redhat.com/en/documentation/red_hat_quay/3.18/html-single/red_hat_quay_api_reference/index#changerepovisibility" format="html" scope="external"><codeph>POST /api/v1/repository/{repository}/changevisibility</codeph></xref> command.</p>
    </context>
    <steps-unordered>
      <step>
        <cmd>You can change the visibility of your repository to public or private by specifying the desired option in the <codeph>visibility</codeph> schema. For example:
</cmd>
        <info>
          <codeblock outputclass="language-terminal">$ curl -X POST \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer &lt;bearer_token&gt;" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "visibility": "private"
  }' \
  "https://quay-server.example.com/api/v1/repository/my_namespace/test_repo_three/changevisibility"</codeblock>
          <p outputclass="title">
            <b>Example output</b>
          </p>
          <codeblock outputclass="language-terminal">{"success": true}</codeblock>
        </info>
      </step>
    </steps-unordered>
  </taskbody>
</task>
